  "contract": "Mok'rash's Circlet equips proc dummy 304007 (worldforged tiers 312980/316980/320980), an aura 42 (proc trigger spell) on the Water Wave records 304008/312981/316981/320981. Every dummy carries Spell.dbc ProcFlags 0 and the world had no spell_proc row, so Aura::GetProcEffectMask found no proc entry and 'When struck in combat by melee attacks you have a chance to inflict ... Frost damage to all enemies within ... yards' never happened (#11662). The records' ProcChance is 100; the three tier tooltips add '(3sec. internal cooldown)' while the base tooltip and DBC name none, so the base dummy keeps Cooldown 0 and the tiers carry 3000. The repair grants the taken melee auto attack and taken melee damage-class masks (ProcFlags 40) for damage at the hit phase and defers Chance to the record. spell_proc_chance reads 100 on every dummy, and aura_proc_rate replays each aura's native incoming proc decision on a synthetic melee strike (always proc) while ranged, spell and outgoing events never do. Real swings by three hostile Horde players then make the wearer cast Water Wave and damage the strikers, and over ten further seconds the tier with its 3 second cooldown casts fewer waves than the uncapped base dummy. Before the repair the chance lookups fail with 'Spell has no proc entry' and every rate and count reads 0, so the discriminating assertions fail rather than flake.",
